  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "Tulaga tonu: ata suesuega tutoatasi, fautuaga polokolo, mo se fakataitaiga fakamatala matala.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "Ne fakatonu se tulaga muamua: ko Belgium (BE) e fakasino nei ki te ggana Tatese kae se te Falani — ko tino tautala Flemish te tokoukega o te fenua (~60%) i lo tino tautala Falani Walloon (~40%).",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "Ne fakatonu se tulaga muamua: ko Kazakhstan (KZ) e fakasino nei ki te ggana Kazakh kae se te Lusia, i te mea kua iai nei se fakaliliuga Kazakh — e tutusa mo te fakatonuga muamua mo Belgium.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Tulafono avanoa mo crawler",
  "Crawler simulator": "Fakataitaiga Crawler",
  "Currency": "Tupe",
  "Custom tier": "Tulaga Totino",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "E lipoti mai ne te Daily Nous se tusitusiga ne toe fakaseaogaina mai te Journal of Medical Ethics, ne aofia i ei ni faasinoga loga ne fakafuafua fua kae \"hallucinated\" ne te AI — faatasi mo fesootaiga iunivesite pepelo mo tuatusi imeli kua seai — kae ne tuku fua ne te tusitala e aunoa mo se fakatonu e ui lava ne tuku se avanoa ke fakatonuina. E fakatusatusa ne te tusitusiga tenei mo te Bioethics, telā e mafai o iloa ne ana faiga fakaotomatika faasinoga te faafitauli tenei — kae e finau me e se ko meafaigaluega mo te ilo te faafitauli tino (ne pupuni ne se polokalama a se tino faimatala a faasinoga pepelo i lalo ifo o se minute), kae ko galuega a tino iloiloga e seai se totogi mo faiga fakasalalauga e taui atili te uke i lo te tonu.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Fakaaogaseseina o fakamatala e aunoa mo se totogi vs. aogaga AI e tau ki tiliona tala",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Ne fakatu ne Demis Hassabis se fakalapotopotoga pule e pei te FINRA mo te tukuatuga o mote AI maluga: e tuku ne fale suesue olotou mote mo te iloiloga e oo atu ki te 30 aso ae mua o te tukuatuga, e loto malie muamua, faatasi mo se ala ki te usiga fakamalosi i te maketi a te US.",
  "Denied": "Fakafitia",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Mote Amataga Tulafono e Mafai o Fakagalueina",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Mote amataga tulafono e mafai o fakagalueina i /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — se saiti tuutino tuutino faatasi mo te vaega katoa e mafai o faitau ne masini, kua sauni mo Cloudflare Pages io me so se hosting tuutino.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Te tukuatuina o tulafono e mafai o faitau ne masini i au saiti",
  "Disclaimer": "Fakailoaga Fakaeteete",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "E kese mai te UI faatino, SEO, io me API tuutino, e tuku ne te AI Ingestion & Capability Layer se fakatulagaga saiti e fakasaga ki masini: se Manifest Layer (puna ulu e pei te /llms.txt mo te /ai/manifest.json), se Corpus Layer (poto e mafai o faitau ne masini), se Capability Layer (meafaigaluega e mafai o valaauina ne sui), mo se Governance Layer (tupuaga, laiseneina, fakalomiga). E fakamuamua te tuutino, kae e mafai o fakamalosia ki API mo MCP. Fakailoa: i te pepa tenei e faaigoa ne te AICL te fakatulagaga ingestion; i itulau polokolo a te saiti tenei e faasino te AICL ki te Vaega Laiseneina Fakamatala AI.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Tusitusiga",
  "Docs / Examples": "Tusitusiga / Fakataitaiga",
  "Document library": "Faletusi Tusitusiga",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "E iai ni aia tatau o te AI — mo a fakatulagaga e talafeagai moni?",
  "Download": "Sii Ifo",
  "Draft status": "Tulaga Ata",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Fakataitaiga aoga: HMAC-SHA256 fakatasi mo se muna faasoa, e fakaasi mai ei token laisene e fakapipii ki talosaga, otiga taimi, mo e mafai o fakamaonia. A token faigaluega moni e tatau o sainia fakatuulua, faatasi mo te ki lautele a te tino tuku e mafai o mauaina i lalo o te /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "E valu isi tusitusiga fou i te /topics, i te taimi tenei ne suesueina ne se sui AI kae se ne filifili lima — e tutusa tulafono mo mua: puna takitasi ne mauaina mo fakamaonia e moni ola, aotelega ko a matou lava tusitusiga, ae mua o faaopoopo so se mea. E 14 katoa.",
  "Email": "Imeli",
